                <pb facs="0253" n="165" sameAs="frus:frus1933v05/pg165"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">825.6374/1115: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Chile</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Culbertson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Santiago</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1933-03-17T10:00:00-04:00">March 17, 1933—10
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received 10:35 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>47. Referring to my telegram No. 46, March 16, 6 p.m. The Minister for Foreign
                    Affairs has not yet completed memorandum. Press this morning reflects a
                    determination of the Government to treat its action as a <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >fait accompli</hi> and to insist upon its position. Indications are that
                    memorandum will contribute nothing to solution and that it will be too long to
                    telegraph. I believe therefore that action need not be delayed awaiting the
                    memorandum which will probably be primarily a defense of the Government’s action
                    and at most a compromise which takes for its starting point the assumption that
                    the Government was justified in diverting the service of the 60 peso charge from
                    the trustees to the Chilean Treasury.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Culbertson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
